---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { rel } from "../lib/rel";
import config from "../site.config.mjs";
const here = Astro.url.pathname;
const mail = config.correctionsContact;
---
<Base title="How it works" current="about" description="How Bethnal Green Live finds and checks its listings.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>How Bethnal Green Live works</h1>
    <p>
      Bethnal Green Live is a free guide to what's on around Bethnal Green, London E2: club nights, gigs, films, food,
      markets and community events, from the streets around the station out to about a twenty-minute walk. Now and then
      we list something further away when it's worth the trip.
    </p>

    <h2>Who finds the listings</h2>
    <p>
      AI agents do the legwork. Every morning they read venue websites and ticket pages, and for every fact they
      record (the date, the time, the price, who's playing) they keep the exact words from the page it came from.
    </p>

    <h2>How they're checked</h2>
    <p>
      A separate checking agent opens every one of those pages again and looks for those exact words. A listing only goes
      up if the name, the venue and the date are all confirmed on the venue's or ticket seller's own page. Anything
      that can't be confirmed is left out rather than guessed. Anything doubtful waits for a person, and a person
      approves every update before it reaches this site.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each event page says when it was checked and links to the pages it was checked against, so you can see for
      yourself. Events in the next fortnight are checked again as they get closer.
    </p>

    <h2>What we don't do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We don't copy promoters' descriptions or photos.</li>
      <li>We don't collect listings from sites whose terms say no, or from social media.</li>
      <li>We don't take money to list things. If that ever changes, paid listings will be clearly labelled.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>If something's wrong</h2>
    <p>
      Plans change, so check the ticket page before you go.
      {mail
        ? <> If you spot a mistake, <a href={mail.includes("@") ? `mailto:${mail}` : mail}>tell us</a> and we'll fix it the same day.</>
        : " A way to report mistakes is coming soon."}
    </p>

    <h2>Never miss a night</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={rel(here, "newsletter.html")}>Get the weekly newsletter</a>, or
      <a href={rel(here, "calendar.html#feeds")}>add the listings to your own calendar</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
